(1) proton decay: need Lambda/sqrt|C| >= 5.10e+15 GeV (tau(1e16)=3.5e+35 yr)
    C=1 (no suppression)                                           1/a >= 5.1e+15 GeV
    C=eps^2, eps=0.13 (X2 link channel, one leakage per light pair) 1/a >= 6.6e+14 GeV
    C=W*eps^4, eps=0.13                                            1/a >= 8.6e+13 GeV
    C=W*eps^4, eps=0.02                                            1/a >= 2.0e+12 GeV
    margin at 1/a = M_Pl=1.22e19 GeV, C=1: tau/bound = 3.3e+13
(2) fermion modes per cell -> qubits with a local 3D encoding (x2..x3)
    one qubit (axiom literal)                               modes 1  qubits ~2..3
    X2 walker package (2 x 16), all 3 generations           modes 32  qubits ~64..96
    KS/staggered 16-carrier (F6:147)                        modes 16  qubits ~32..48
    C5 gravity root (panel F: ~22.5 Dirac fields x 4)       modes 90  qubits ~180..270
    F4/X1 slab 3x16x4xL, L=4..6                             modes 768..1152  qubits ~1536..3456
    exact on-site G_SM forces the mode space at a cell to contain every multiplet: >= 16 modes per Weyl component per generation
